// BulkValidateRow One line of the NDJSON response to a bulk dry run. `status` discriminates the four outcomes: `valid` (the row would be created and published), `invalid` (the row carries model errors, see `fields`), `duplicate` (the row's natural key already maps to a published passport, which is echoed unchanged) and `error` (the line could not be read). Results come back in input order and `row` numbers them from one, so no identifier is needed to correlate them.
